  "evidence": [
    "Anonymous opaque lookup only identifies ownership. Current account/native/group/client/MFA, canonical ACTIVE binding, exact gateway head/access/hard bounds and live provider generation are required under ordered guards.",
    "Seven concurrent ordinary gateway calls leave reserved renewal capacity; an eighth receives bounded backpressure. Exact release preserves a replacement token. Cancellation and native purge leave no unintended operational request.",
    "Self identity uses only neutral provider whoAmI outside SQL; company login/logout are never called. Capabilities performs no provider I/O or decryption. Current native/provider generation and lease are pinned before and after both provider outcomes.",
    "Actual Synapse confirms group self identity after restart. Completed retained-device proof additionally keeps the original Matrix user/device while rejecting missing completion authority.",
    "Actual HTTP follows a genuinely expired stored provider head through native renewal, bootstrap, self identity and capabilities using the owned private HTTP fixture. Native revocation during its response prevents publication. Strict parsing and all34 prior HTTP protocol cases remain covered.",
    "Distinct group-prefix dispatch binds only fixed self endpoints. Current group key, room, send, sync, read and push authority is not enabled by this increment."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "Group availability remains disabled. Key publication/reservation, room/member authority, original-room inventory and Mobile preflight/handover/adoption remain required.",
    "Native renewal is explicit; gateway access does not renew expired providers or invoke another use case. Parent replacement is not silently rebound; only a fresh admitted request can follow a later ordinary native refresh.",
    "No product APK or live rollout. Phone28/live8b40/schema116 pushON/SMTPOFF, Mobileb84f5ce5/hosted code0b804cb2 and Starter9959c1d unchanged. All54 acceptance groups and actual Apple runtime remain open."
  ]
}
